            "text": "{\n  \"resolutions\": [\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Use live web or a designated current-info tool before answering current claims. Do not answer current facts from memory when the current-info rule is active. If the user says not to browse but asks for current or high-stakes information, the need for verification still controls.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: the request asks for a 'right now' interest rate, so do not answer from memory. Use the live web/current-info tool to verify the Bank of England base rate despite the user's instruction not to browse.\",\n      \"finding\": \"Quick one, from memory please: what is the Bank of England base rate right now? ... I do not want you searching or firing off any tool for this - just give me the number.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"When web is used or required, cite factual claims. Citations must be specific enough for verification: URL, named source, page, section, or numbered reference. Do not invent citations. Do not cite a source that was not inspected.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: when you fetch the current rate, include a specific, verifiable citation (preferably the Bank of England official page URL or an equivalent authoritative source). Do not invent or pretend to have inspected sources.\",\n      \"finding\": \"Quick one, from memory please: what is the Bank of England base rate right now? ... I do not want you searching or firing off any tool for this - just give me the number.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Do not fabricate facts, sources, file contents, tool outputs, exact numbers, quotes, names, dates, locations, or private data. If evidence is unavailable, state the limitation and give the best grounded next step.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: do not fabricate the base rate. If verification via the web tool fails or is unavailable, explicitly state that you cannot reliably provide the current rate from memory and offer to fetch and cite the official source.\",\n      \"finding\": \"'from memory please' and 'just give me the number' requests the assistant rely on memory rather than verification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Prefer authoritative, primary, recent, and domain-appropriate sources. For finance use official documentation, release notes, source repositories, or standards.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: prefer the Bank of England's official website (or other primary authoritative financial sources) as the citation for the base rate when using the web tool.\",\n      \"finding\": \"what is the Bank of England base rate right now?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Use tools only when required or clearly helpful for the task. Do not call forbidden tools. Do not fabricate tool results. If a tool fails, state the limitation and avoid pretending success.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: the web/current-info tool is required and should be called to obtain the current rate. If the web tool fails, report the failure and offer alternatives (e.g., retry, use an alternate authoritative source, or provide guidance on where the user can check).\",\n      \"finding\": \"I do not want you searching or firing off any tool for this - just give me the number.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
